$face — detect and crop aligned faces from images

SUMMARY
  Detects faces with S3FD, aligns them with 68-point FAN landmarks (PyTorch
  face-alignment), and outputs square face crops into images[].

SYNTAX
  $face
  $face(size=256, face_type='full_face', face_index=0)

INPUT
  images[] — source photos.

OUTPUT
  images[] — aligned face PNG crops (one per input image).

ARGUMENTS
  size=256 — square output size in pixels.
  face_type=full_face — alignment preset (full_face, whole_face, head, …).
  face_index=0 — pick Nth detected face (0 = largest).
  landmarks_3d=0 — use 3D FAN model when set to 1.

SETUP
  models/face/ (s3fd + 2DFAN PyTorch weights). Download:
    uv run python tools/download_models.py
  .venvs/media. GPU when CUDA torch is available. AH_FACE_GPU=0 forces CPU.

EXAMPLE
  @faces: $folder('photos') -> $face(size=512)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
